  "body": "Native-export path validation now repeats slash-delimited segments without ambiguous repetition, preserving the accepted path rules. Identity and published-link test helpers parse URLs and compare origins or hostnames exactly instead of accepting URL substrings.\n\nThe change records the intentional Base-copy adaptation and regenerates the source lock. No contract judgments or generated acceptance views change.\n\nValidation: TypeScript, the existing native identity journey, the existing public catalogue journey against the built Worker, syntax and source-integrity checks, and targeted path/link mutation checks. The path comparison covers 19,531 short inputs and 1,000 maximum-length invalid paths. Exact-SHA branch Verify supplies the full suite.\n\nBase publication inspection is COMPLETE/PASS with zero blocking findings on the committed tree. Exact-SHA Verify is still in progress after the bounded five-minute polling window: https://github.com/just-every/run-lamp/actions/runs/44108731182. This PR does not claim READY or landing.",
